# One canonical host. https://openbiblestories.org is canonical (it is the
# `site` in astro.config.mjs, the canonical/hreflang/JSON-LD URLs, and the
# sitemap); www is 301'd to it so search signals aren't split across two
# hosts. Cloudflare Pages honors absolute-URL sources here as long as BOTH
# hostnames are attached to the Pages project as custom domains — if www is
# not attached, this rule never fires. Host rules must come first.
https://www.openbiblestories.org/*  https://openbiblestories.org/:splat  301

# Archived pages (Library browser removed in favor of /discover/, which has
# its own search, format filters, and inline reader). These keep old
# bookmarks/links/search results from 404ing. Deep links like
# /library/#code--team are preserved by the browser (the fragment survives a
# redirect) and discover.js opens the language from the hash.
/create/library/*  /discover/  301
/library           /discover/  301
/library/*         /discover/  301

# The Why OBS page moved from /features/ to /why-obs/ to match its nav label;
# the standalone /resources/ page was folded into the Translate page's
# Resources tab.
/features/*   /why-obs/              301
/resources/*  /translate/#resources  301

# The standalone reader at /discover/read/ (and /{locale}/discover/read/ in
# all 16 locales) was retired in the previous release: stories are static
# pages now, and the reader is mounted in place on each language hub. Those
# URLs were live until then, so Google has them — and without these rules
# they 404 rather than redirecting, which is what Search Console's
# "Not found (404)" is reporting.
#
# Both go to the locale's own Discover page: it is the page that now leads to
# every story, and it keeps the visitor in the language they arrived in. A 301
# preserves the fragment, and discover.js already forwards a legacy language
# hash to that language's hub, so an old deep link still lands on the right
# language.
/discover/read/          /discover/           301
/discover/read           /discover/           301
/:locale/discover/read/  /:locale/discover/   301
/:locale/discover/read   /:locale/discover/   301

# @astrojs/sitemap used to emit sitemap-0.xml; the sitemap is now an index
# (sitemap-index.xml → sitemap-pages.xml + sitemap-languages.xml). Keep the
# old URL alive for crawlers that still hold it. Safe to remove in 2027.
/sitemap-0.xml  /sitemap-pages.xml  301
